  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to NCI-H2196, suggesting a complex but interconnected pathway. The evidence indicates that Mollicellin N interacts with Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and this compound further targets NCI-H2196. Similarly, Mollicellin N also interacts with A704, which is a target of the same compound, reinforcing the role of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid in the pathway. Additionally, Mollicellin N is linked to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a different compound that also leads to NCI-H2196. These findings suggest that Mollicellin N may act through multiple distinct mechanisms, each involving a different target, ultimately contributing to the interaction with NCI-H2196. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mollicellin N to exert its biological effects through various molecular routes, underscoring its broad pharmacological profile.",
